# PHOENIX - Master Project Rule

## The Goal

Build an automated cricket betting system that learns to make consistent profits over time. The system scrapes live odds from **LotusBook** (`https://lotusbook.site/cricket`), trains a **reinforcement learning agent** through virtual betting, and only graduates to real money once profitability is proven.

**We are NOT building a rule-based betting system.** We are building a self-improving RL agent that discovers profitable betting behavior through experience.

## How We Achieve It

```
1. SCRAPE live odds from LotusBook (Playwright, every 3-5 seconds)
2. ENRICH with raw match statistics (Cricbuzz: score, wickets, overs, run rate)
3. ENGINEER 66 data-backed features (odds momentum, volatility, microstructure, raw stats, portfolio)
4. TRAIN an RL agent (PPO via Stable-Baselines3) on a custom Gymnasium environment
5. VIRTUAL BET until the agent proves: >55% win rate, >8% ROI, >1.5 Sharpe over 14 days
6. GRADUATE to live execution only after human approval
```

**DATA-ONLY PHILOSOPHY:** Every feature must be either raw data from LotusBook/Cricbuzz, a mathematical transformation of that data, or the agent's own portfolio state. NO cricket domain heuristics, NO subjective judgments, NO hand-coded patterns. The RL agent discovers all patterns from data.

## Architecture (6 Layers)

- **Layer 1 - Data:** LotusBook scraper + Cricbuzz enricher -> Redis pub/sub -> TimescaleDB
- **Layer 2 - Features:** 66-feature observation vector (odds, momentum, raw stats, portfolio state)
- **Layer 3 - RL Engine:** Gymnasium env + PPO agent + reward shaping + curriculum learning
- **Layer 4 - Execution:** Virtual bet engine + risk manager + [live executor post-graduation]
- **Layer 5 - API:** FastAPI backend + WebSocket streaming
- **Layer 6 - Dashboard:** Next.js 14 (training curves, P&L charts, graduation progress)

## Tech Stack

- **Python 3.11+**, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy (async), Pydantic v2
- **RL:** Stable-Baselines3, Gymnasium, PyTorch
- **Scraping:** Playwright (CDP WebSocket interception)
- **Database:** TimescaleDB (time-series), Redis 7 (pub/sub + cache)
- **Frontend:** Next.js 14, Tailwind CSS, Recharts, TypeScript
- **Infra:** Docker Compose, Prometheus, Grafana
- **Quality:** ruff, mypy, pytest, pre-commit, structlog

